# PALINDORME XR — Spatial Computing Launcher & Stereo Environment

**Revision 3** · Product & Architecture Plan (adds Hand Interaction)

PALINDORME XR turns an ordinary Android phone, placed in a passive smartphone VR headset, into a stereoscopic spatial launcher with floating windows. It opens straight into a dual-viewport OpenGL ES 3.0 home with **3-DOF rotational head tracking**, gaze-dwell and Bluetooth gamepad input, experimental monocular camera passthrough, and optional ARCore world perception (which also enables limited 6-DOF positional tracking on supported devices).

---

## 0. What Changed in This Revision

| Area | Change | Why |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| Terminology | "6-DOF-style rotational tracking" → **3-DOF rotational** by default; **6-DOF only in ARCore mode** | The original claim was contradictory and over-promised. |
| Feasibility | ARCore moved from "no 6-DOF" to **"6-DOF via ARCore, device-dependent"** | ARCore motion tracking gives positional tracking. Phone-in-headset use is experimental because of lens-box occlusion and rear-camera framing. |
| Window rendering | Replaced "Compose PlayerSurface" with **`SurfaceTexture` + `lockHardwareCanvas` / direct `setVideoSurface`**; added **touch-injection layer** | A WebView or Compose view cannot render to a GL texture on its own, and Compose's `PlayerSurface` is an on-screen surface. |
| Sensors | Prefer **`TYPE_GAME_ROTATION_VECTOR`**, add prediction, add `HIGH_SAMPLING_RATE_SENSORS` | Avoids magnetometer drift/jumps in headsets (magnets). Android 12+ throttles sensors to 200 Hz without the permission. |
| Performance | Added **frame budgets, ADPF hint sessions, sustained-performance mode, thermal tiers** | A phone in a headset throttles fast; this is the main product risk. |
| Comfort & safety | New **comfort & motion-sickness section** | The original covered only the passthrough warning. |
| Testing | Robolectric alone replaced by a **layered test strategy** | Robolectric cannot execute OpenGL. |
| New sections | Non-goals, performance budgets, risk register, acceptance criteria, privacy, accessibility, device matrix | Needed for sign-off. |
| Versions | Marked as **"pin and verify at Stage 1 kickoff"** | Dependency versions should come from the actual build, not memory. |
| **Hand interaction (Rev 3)** | New **Hand Interaction System** (Section 5.8): camera-based hand tracking, "look + pinch" selection, pinch-drag, two-hand resize, palm menu | Apple Vision Pro and Galaxy XR style controls, adapted honestly to a phone with one rear camera and no eye tracking. |

