## 2. Feasibility Classification & Scope

| Capability | Class | Reality on ordinary phones |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| Side-by-side stereo rendering, lens distortion, IPD/FOV calibration, 6 procedural environments, window manager (move/depth/resize/minimize), gaze dwell, app library via `<queries>`, DataStore settings, telemetry | **Fully implementable** | Needs only GPU, `Display`, `PackageManager`. |
| 3-DOF head tracking, Bluetooth gamepad, Photo Picker gallery, Media3 playback, voice commands | **Needs compatible hardware** | Needs gyroscope (or rotation-vector sensor), a paired controller, microphone and speech service. Fallbacks: touch-drag look, gamepad look. |
| Monocular camera passthrough, 3D overlay on camera feed, ARCore planes/anchors/light estimation, ARCore Depth | **Experimental** | One rear camera gives a flat feed, no stereo depth. Passthrough latency is typically well above dedicated headsets, so stationary use only. ARCore needs Google Play Services for AR and a supported device; depth is device-dependent. |
| **ARCore 6-DOF positional tracking in the headset** | **Experimental / device-dependent** | Works only if the camera has a usable view (many headsets block or offset it). Auto-disabled with a clear message when tracking quality stays poor. |
| **Camera-based hand tracking and gestures** (pinch, drag, two-hand resize, palm menu) | **Experimental / needs compatible hardware** | Needs the rear camera to see your hands, which means a headset with a camera cutout or open front, decent lighting, and a phone fast enough to run on-device hand landmark inference at ~30 fps. Landmarks come from one camera, so depth is estimated from hand size, not measured. Falls back to gaze dwell and gamepad whenever hands are unavailable. |
| Stereo dual-camera passthrough, hosting live third-party app UIs inside 3D windows | **Not reproducible** | One camera cannot give two eye views; Android sandboxing blocks embedding other apps. Launching an app hands foreground to Android. |

### Non-Goals
- No mirroring/capturing other apps' screens (would need `MediaProjection`, a sensitive capability, and still not interactive).
- No positional tracking without ARCore.
- No Google Cardboard SDK dependency (deprecated; lens profile logic is our own).
- No networked/multi-user features, accounts, or analytics SDKs.
- No eye tracking (phones don't have it); "look" is head-gaze.
- No full finger-level mid-air typing or sculpting precision; hand control targets selection, dragging, scrolling, resizing and poking large controls.
- No claim of Apple Vision Pro / Galaxy XR parity: no stereo hand depth, no gaze-and-hand latency at their level, and no sensors beyond the phone's.

### Honesty Guarantees
- **No dead-end affordances**: every dock button, window type, preset and slider does real work; unsupported features are hidden or shown disabled with the reason.
- **No broad permissions**: no `QUERY_ALL_PACKAGES` (use targeted `<queries>`), no `READ_EXTERNAL_STORAGE`/`READ_MEDIA_*` (use Photo Picker and SAF).
- **Permissions requested only in context**: `CAMERA` at first passthrough, `RECORD_AUDIO` at first voice opt-in, `HIGH_SAMPLING_RATE_SENSORS` is a normal (install-time) permission.

