## 6. Staged Delivery

### Stage 1 — Core Spatial VR Launcher
Adaptive icon, bundled fonts, module contracts, `StereoRenderingEngine`, `HeadTrackingEngine`, `InputInteractionManager` (gaze, gamepad, opt-in voice), `SpatialWindowManager` + `VirtualContentHost`, `SpatialKeyboard`, windows (Browser, Media3 Player, App Library, Gallery, Settings, glTF viewer, Info), six environments, Compose hub, `PerformanceMonitor`, `ComfortManager`.

**Acceptance**
- Cold start → stereo home in < 2.5 s on the reference device.
- Head pose updates within 1 frame; re-center works.
- Calibration changes persist and apply live.
- Each window type opens, moves, resizes, minimizes and closes without leaks (LeakCanary clean).
- Gamepad can operate every control; gaze can operate every control.
- Green Gradle build; unit and instrumented tests pass.

### Stage 2 — Experimental Monocular Passthrough & Hand Control
`SharedCameraFrameSource`, `HandTrackingEngine`, `GestureRecognizer`, `HandRayInteractor`, hand setup/calibration flow, skeleton overlay, haptic/audio feedback, the "Hands off" toggle, and the gaze fallback logic (Section 5.8). Stage 1 ships gaze dwell and gamepad only; hand control builds on the Stage 1 `InputInteractionManager` event interface, so no Stage 1 rework is needed. Safety dialog, runtime permission with rationale and revocation recovery, `CameraEngine` with OES quad, brightness/exposure/resolution controls, lens-distortion correction of the camera feed (optional) so real-world edges aren't doubly warped.

**Acceptance**
- Denied/revoked permission falls back to an environment in < 1 s with an explanation.
- Backgrounding and returning restores the preview.
- Passthrough latency measured and shown in diagnostics.
- Look + Pinch selects the correct target on ≥ 95 % of 100 scripted trials per device (recorded hand-landmark replay for CI, live trials on device).
- No false pinches in a 5-minute "hands resting / gesturing while talking" replay; false-positive rate target < 1 per minute.
- Hand tracking end-to-end latency (camera frame → gesture event) measured and shown in diagnostics; target ≤ 80 ms.
- Losing the camera, hands, or permission falls back to gaze dwell in < 1.5 s with a visible indicator.
- "Hands off" toggle disables hand input immediately and leaves the camera closed if passthrough is also off.
- Green build and tests.

### Stage 3 — Optional ARCore & Release Packaging
`ARPerceptionEngine` (`checkAvailability`, install prompt flow), coordinator switch, planes, light estimation, depth occlusion (if supported), anchors, optional 6-DOF positional tracking with a tracking-quality indicator and auto-fallback to 3-DOF.

**Acceptance**
- 100 consecutive A↔B switches without a camera error; hand tracking resumes correctly after each switch (or falls back with a note when ARCore has priority).
- Unsupported devices show a clear VR-only state; no ARCore classes load.
- Signed release APK and debug APK build; `lint` and `R8` release build verified; app size reported.
- Documents delivered: Feasibility, Architecture, Honest 3-State Testing.

