## 7. Testing Strategy

| Layer | Tool | Covers |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| Pure logic unit tests | JUnit | Quaternion math, filters, prediction, raycasts, distortion mesh generation, window placement/limits, settings migrations, state machines |
| Android-framework tests | Robolectric | DataStore, app discovery with `<queries>`, permission flows, coordinator state machine |
| GL correctness | Instrumented tests on device/emulator with software GL | Shader compile/link, FBO completeness, golden-image tests for each environment and the distortion mesh |
| UI | Compose UI tests | Settings, calibration, permission rationale |
| Device runs | Manual + scripted on matrix | Latency, thermal, battery, sensor quality |
| Soak | 30-min automated run | Memory growth, GL object leaks, thermal tiering |
| Gesture logic | JUnit with recorded landmark traces | Pinch hysteresis, tap vs. hold, drag target-lock, two-hand resize, palm-open, handedness mirroring, dropout and recovery |
| Hand tracking on device | Manual + scripted | Latency, accuracy under bright/dim light, different skin tones and hand sizes, sleeves and rings, hands near frame edges, thermal and battery with inference running |

**Device matrix (minimum)**: a low-RAM Android 7–9 phone, a mid-range Android 11–12, a flagship Android 14+, a phone without gyroscope (fallback), a phone with ARCore and one without, one with a 120 Hz display, and one with a notch/cutout.

**Honest 3-State Testing document** records each feature as: *Verified on device* · *Verified in emulator/unit only* · *Not tested* — never merged.

