## 8. Risk Register

| Risk | Likelihood | Impact | Mitigation |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| Thermal throttling in a closed headset | High | High | Adaptive tiers, ADPF, 60 Hz fallback, break prompts |
| High motion-to-photon latency → nausea | Medium | High | Prediction, low-latency render path, render-scale first |
| WebView/Compose hardware-canvas quirks on some OEMs | Medium | Medium | Software fallback, window cap, device-specific allowlist |
| Phone screen resolution too low for legible text | High | Medium | 20 sp minimum, large-text mode, bold glass UI |
| ARCore unusable in headset (camera blocked) | High | Low | Auto-detect poor tracking, fall back to 3-DOF |
| Sensor drift / no gyro | Medium | Medium | Game rotation vector, recenter, touch/gamepad look |
| Play Store policy issues (camera, queries) | Low | High | Targeted `<queries>`, in-context permissions, privacy policy |
| Dependency drift | Medium | Medium | Version catalog, CI check |
| Headset blocks the rear camera, so hands can't be seen | High | Medium | Detect during setup; keep gaze/gamepad as full equivalents; document headsets known to work |
| Hand inference too slow / hot on mid-range phones | High | High | Adaptive hand tier, idle gating, single-hand mode, auto-disable with banner |
| False pinches cause accidental actions | Medium | Medium | Hysteresis, debounce, confidence gate, confirmation for destructive actions, "Hands off" toggle |
| Monocular depth error makes push/pull and poke inaccurate | High | Low | Gaze-first targeting, calibrated palm width, depth gestures clamped and eased, poke limited to large targets |
| Uneven tracking across skin tones, lighting, hand sizes | Medium | High | Test across diverse users and lighting; show hints; never gate essential actions on hands |

