## 9. Open Questions for You
1. Is the target primarily personal/sideload use or Play Store distribution? (Affects privacy policy, review effort, and signing.)
2. Should the Browser allow any site, or ship with a curated start page and optional content filter?
3. Is DRM video (Netflix-like) in scope? (Not feasible with the surface-capture approach; the plan assumes no.)
4. Which devices do you actually own for testing? The matrix above should be trimmed to what you can run.
5. Which headset(s) will you use? Hand control only works if the headset leaves the rear camera uncovered (a cutout or open front), so this decides whether hand control is a headline feature or a bonus.
6. Is MediaPipe's on-device hand model acceptable, or do you want a different tracker (smaller, custom-trained, or licensed)?
7. Should "Look + Pinch" be the default input out of the box when a hand is detected, or should gaze dwell remain the default until the user opts in?